From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom-smbchg: do not drive OTG VBUS against an input

The OTG boost was enabled whenever a consumer asked, even with a charger or
a powered dock already supplying VBUS. A dual-role port can be in host mode
under such a source (a dock that powers the phone), and the DWC3 enables
its VBUS regulator on every switch to host. Refuse with -EBUSY while USB
input is present, so two sources never drive VBUS.

---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
@@ -704,6 +704,16 @@
 
 	dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Enabling OTG VBUS regulator");
 
+	/*
+	 * Never drive VBUS against an external source: a powered dock or a
+	 * charger already supplies it, and the USB controller may still be put
+	 * in host mode on such a port.
+	 */
+	if (smbchg_usb_is_present(chip)) {
+		dev_info(chip->dev, "USB input present, not enabling OTG VBUS\n");
+		return -EBUSY;
+	}
+
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
 				 chip->base + SMBCHG_BAT_IF_CMD_CHG, OTG_EN_BIT,
 				 OTG_EN_BIT);
